## 3-Tier Readiness Gate Model

Plans progress through three independent readiness tiers. Each tier has its own gate sequence.
A plan may only require gates from one tier (e.g., a pure code chore only needs C5), or from
multiple tiers (e.g., a deployment feature needs C5 + D3).

```
Code Readiness (C):       C0 → C1 → C2 → C3 → C4 → C5
Deployment Readiness (D): D1 → D2 → D3 → D4 → D5
Business Readiness (B):   B1 → B2 → B3 → B4 → B5 → B6
```

### Gate Quick Reference

| Code | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| C1 | Implementation complete |
| C2 | Unit tests passing |
| C3 | Linter + Codex (ruff, basedpyright) |
| C4 | Full quality-gates.sh |
| C5 | Quickmerge — merged to staging/main |

| Deployment | Meaning |
|-----------|---------|
| D2 | CI/GHA smoke — emulators/mocks, **no real service calls** |
| D3 | Staging SIT — **real service/API calls**, live credentials |
| D4 | Load tests in staging |
| D5 | Production-ready |

| Business | Meaning |
|---------|---------|
| B3 | KPIs met (ML accuracy, P&L, execution alpha, latency — declared per plan) |
| B4 | Batch vs live validation (t+1) |
| B5 | Staging vs live parity (N-min replay) |
| B6 | User approved |

## Current Epic: Code Completion (epic-code-completion)

All plans must reach C5 for all repos in `repo_gates`. This is the first epic gate.

Exception: Plans of type `infra` or `deployment` must also reach D3 regardless of the active epic.

## Archive Criteria

| Type | Archive gate |
|------|-------------|
| `code` | C5 for all `repo_gates` repos |
| `infra` / `deployment` | D3 for all `repo_gates` repos |
| `business` | B6 + domain B3 KPIs |
| `mixed` | Highest required gate across types |

## Pipeline Stages (Updated)

1. **Plans** — PM manifest, active plans index with `completion_gates`, epic assignment
2. **Code (C1–C5)** — implementation → unit tests → linter → quality-gates → quickmerge
3. **Deployment (D1–D5)** — infra → CI smoke → staging SIT → load tests → production
4. **Business (B1–B6)** — criteria → scenarios → KPIs → batch/live validation → user sign-off

